#: ui/NamePage.qml:193
msgid ""
"This module writes nothing into the keyboard. Both buttons only open a "
"terminal where akmctl shows the exact bytes, saves the current name, runs "
"the pre-flight (one administrator authentication to read the Bluetooth "
"channel size), then asks you to type ECRIRE and the name again before its "
"single write."
msgstr ""

#: ui/NamePage.qml:203
msgid ""
"Writing into the keyboard's firmware carries two risks that are not "
"measured: how the firmware answers the write (U5), and whether the name "
"survives a battery change (U3). Have a second working keyboard at hand. The "
"terminal saves the current name first and shows the exact rollback command; "
"the keyboard must be switched off and on afterwards so the name is read "
"back. Details: docs/RENOMMER-CLAVIER.md §5.3 and §6."
msgstr ""

